{
  "artifact": "ws4_chain_119m",
  "artifact_version": "1.0.0",
  "caveats": [
    "The 119 Mm3 schedule is a whole-block arithmetic verification, not a sustainable harvest, AAC, policy result, or investment case.",
    "Blocks are selected whole. Provincial achieved volume can overshoot the control target by the volume of the final block because no block is split, scaled, or fabricated.",
    "Fragment volumes are 990-m forest-area fragments multiplied by their RSYC group curve at the exact integer fragment age. They are not operable, tenure, or economically feasible volumes.",
    "The managed track shares the natural RSYC curve; the simulation applies one CC treatment at offset 0 and does not model planting response, silviculture, fertilization, or genetic gain.",
    "Product and residue values apply frozen chain v5.1 per-province coefficients to WS4 harvest by origin province. Facility assignment, mill capacity, transport, and interprovincial trade are not re-run.",
    "The scaled basis uses one national scale factor to preserve WS4 provincial shares and match the 118.9773391 Mm3 control total; it is not a per-province target-scaling exercise.",
    "Process residue and harvest residue are separate streams. PJ values use the frozen 18.5 GJ/ODT lower heating value; 0.60 harvest recovery is a reference case, not a calibrated recovery factor.",
    "No official OSeCAN file or public OSeCAN surface is changed."
  ],
